# Windows Troubleshooting Lab

## Objective
Learn how to identify and troubleshoot common Windows performance and system issues.

## Tools Used
- Windows 11
- Task Manager
- Device Manager
- Event Viewer
- Disk Management
- PowerShell
- Command Prompt

## Scenario
A Windows computer was experiencing slow performance.

## Troubleshooting Process
1. Checked CPU usage.
2. Checked memory usage.
3. Checked disk usage.
4. Reviewed startup applications.
5. Reviewed Windows Event Viewer.
6. Verified system configuration.

## Result
Identified potential causes of the performance issue and documented the troubleshooting process.

## What I Learned
I learned how to use built-in Windows tools to investigate system problems.
